","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T22:59:54Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T23:13:23Z","body":"> How does one say a set of tags is rare?\r\n\r\nI'm assuming that since Audacity and `dr_wav` don't support them, very few people use or care about them.\r\nAlso, the original code doesn't even cover all tags (there is a total of 22 types, #99504 added support for 14 of them, and Audacity/`dr_wav` supports the 9 types I left in.\r\n\r\n*Maybe I'm trying to prevent a very old PR of mine, older than the one that added tags, from becoming compatibility breaking.*\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978424792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978448990","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107605#issuecomment-2978448990","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107605","id":2978448990,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xh4Ze","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T23:16:07Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T23:16:26Z","body":"Hm radical idea, is it possible to do the godot engine strategy of common cases and low level advanced access. Like we have no tags and let people query if they want to find some","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978448990/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978461967","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107605#issuecomment-2978461967","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107605","id":2978461967,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xh7kP","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T23:25:23Z","updated_at":"2025-06-17T00:39:19Z","body":"> Hm radical idea, is it possible to do the godot engine strategy of common cases and low level advanced access. Like we have no tags and let people query if they want to find some\r\n\r\nThat would probably be possible if AudioStreamWAV importing pulled the entire file data like it's done for MP3 and Ogg Vorbis. Unfortunately that's not the case. AudioStreamWAV is like its own format, and what the load function does is \"convert\" a WAV file to one of them.\r\n\r\nThat was actually my motivation for making #96545, as it could make implementing many things much easier and prevent PRs like this one from ever having existed. AIFF support was just a convenient thing that could be enabled with very few lines over it.\r\n\r\nAnd tag reading on load is already implemented, but it's broken, and this is my take on a fix.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978461967/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978583834","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107605#issuecomment-2978583834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107605","id":2978583834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xiZUa","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-17T00:50:22Z","updated_at":"2025-06-17T00:50:22Z","body":"I'm confused what the actual bugfix is. Is there a way to make this change without refactoring the tag lookup to a dictionary, and without removing some tag types? I understand you don't use them, but if we want to change this decision, we would probably need to get into a discussion with Luna and others and that makes this not a simple bugfix.\r\n\r\nFrom what I can tell, the actual bugfix is a bounds check and &1 padding byte check. If so, I would prefer to make this change far simpler without the refactor of remap handling. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978583834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978840453","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107605#issuecomment-2978840453","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107605","id":2978840453,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xjX-F","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6